jets(ZZ,QuotientRing) -- the jets of an affine algebra
******************************************************

  * Function: *note jets: jets,
  * Usage: 
        jets (n,Q)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * Q, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: jets_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, Option for jets
  * Outputs:
      * a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, 

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note Jets: Top,.  Forms the jets of a
*note QuotientRing: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing, by forming the quotient of
*note jets(ZZ,PolynomialRing): jets_lpZZ_cmPolynomialRing_rp, of the ambient
ring of Q with *note jets(ZZ,Ideal): jets_lpZZ_cmIdeal_rp, of the ideal
defining Q

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(y^2-x^3);                                                |
|                                                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = R/I;                                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : JQ = jets(2,Q);                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : describe JQ                                                        |
|                                                                        |
|                          QQ[x0, y0][x1, y1][x2, y2]                    |
|o5 = -------------------------------------------------------------------|
|           2                    2     2       2                 3     2 |
|     (- 3x0 x2 + 2y0*y2 - 3x0*x1  + y1 , - 3x0 x1 + 2y0*y1, - x0  + y0 )|
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Forming quotients triggers a Groebner basis computation, which may be time
consuming.



Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note jets(ZZ,QuotientRing): jets_lpZZ_cmQuotientRing_rp, -- the jets of an
    affine algebra
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

