jets(ZZ,Graph) -- the jets of a graph
*************************************

  * Function: *note jets: jets,
  * Usage: 
        jets (n,G)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, undirected, finite, and simple
        graph or hypergraph
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: jets_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, Option for jets
  * Outputs:
      * a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, the (hyper)graph of n-jets of G

Description
===========

This function is provided by the package *note Jets: Top,.

Jets of graphs are defined in § 2 of F. Galetto, E. Helmick, and M. Walsh, Jet
graphs (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.08933 ). The input is of type *note
Graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph, as defined by the *note EdgeIdeals: (EdgeIdeals)Top,
package, which is automatically exported when loading *note Jets: Top,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph(R,{{x,y},{y,z}})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{x, y}, {y, z}}}                                      |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {x, y, z}                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : JG = jets(2,G)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{x1, y1}, {y1, z1}, {y2, x0}, {y1, x0}, {x2, y0}, {z2,|
|           "ring" => QQ[x2, y2, z2, x1, y1, z1, x0, y0, z0]                  |
|           "vertices" => {x2, y2, z2, x1, y1, z1, x0, y0, z0}                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y0}, {x1, y0}, {z1, y0}, {x0, y0}, {y2, z0}, {y1, z0}, {y0, z0}}}            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : vertexCovers JG                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {y2*y1*y0, x2*z2*x1*z1*x0*z0, y1*x0*y0*z0, x1*z1*x0*y0*z0}              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We can also calculate the jets of a  *note HyperGraph: (EdgeIdeals)HyperGraph,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[u,v,w,x,y,z]                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : H = hyperGraph(R,{{u},{v,w},{x,y,z}})                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{u}, {v, w}, {x, y, z}}}                         |
|                "ring" => R                                                  |
|                "vertices" => {u, v, w, x, y, z}                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : HyperGraph                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : jets(1,H)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{u1}, {u0}, {w1, v0}, {v1, w0}, {v0, w0}, {z1, x0|
|                "ring" => QQ[u1, v1, w1, x1, y1, z1, u0, v0, w0, x0, y0, z0] |
|                "vertices" => {u1, v1, w1, x1, y1, z1, u0, v0, w0, x0, y0, z0|
|                                                                             |
|o7 : HyperGraph                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|, y0}, {y1, x0, z0}, {x1, y0, z0}, {x0, y0, z0}}}                            |
|                                                                             |
|}                                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Rings of jets are usually constructed as towers of rings with tiers
corresponding to jets of different orders. However, the tower is flattened out
before constructing the edge ideal of the jets of a (hyper)graph. This is done
in order to ensure compatibility with the *note EdgeIdeals: (EdgeIdeals)Top,
package.





Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note jets(ZZ,Graph): jets_lpZZ_cmGraph_rp, -- the jets of a graph
  * "jets(ZZ,HyperGraph)"
