liftingFunction -- compute values of a lifting function
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        liftingFunction(s,j,k)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a natural number
      * j, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a natural number
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a natural number
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of cardinality $k$
        lifts of a cardinality $j$ set under depolarization

Description
===========

This function was added in version 1.2 of the package *note Jets: Top,.

Given a set $X$ and a natural number $s$, let $\mathcal{J}_s (X)$ be the set
that contains the elements $x_0,\dots,x_s$ for every element $x\in X$. The
depolarization map $\delta_s \colon \mathcal{J}_s (X)\to X$ is defined by
$\delta_s (x_i) = x$ for every $x\in X$ and $i\in \{0,\dots,s\}$.

The lifting function $l_s (j,k)$ counts the number of subsets $V\subseteq
\mathcal{J}_s (X)$ of cardinality $k$ such that $\delta_s (V) = U$, where
$U\subseteq X$ is a fixed subset of cardinality $j$. Note that this number does
not depend on $U$ but only on its cardinality. See F. Galetto, N. Iammarino,
and T. Yu, Jets and principal components of monomial ideals, and very
well-covered graphs (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01836 ) for computing this
function.

+---------------------------+
|i1 : liftingFunction(1,2,3)|
|                           |
|o1 = 4                     |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : liftingFunction(2,2,3)|
|                           |
|o2 = 18                    |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : liftingFunction(1,3,2)|
|                           |
|o3 = 0                     |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : liftingFunction(1,0,0)|
|                           |
|o4 = 1                     |
+---------------------------+

For uses of the lifting function, see *note Example 4: Example 4,.

* Menu:

* liftingMatrix::               arrange values of lifting function in a matrix

Ways to use liftingFunction:
============================

  * "liftingFunction(ZZ,ZZ,ZZ)"

