Example 3 -- jets of determinantal varieties
********************************************

Consider the determinantal varieties $X_r$ of $3\times 3$ matrices of rank at
most $r$, which are defined by the vanishing of minors of size $r+1$.  We
illustrate computationally some of the known results about jets.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_(1,1)..x_(3,3)]   |
|                                |
|o1 = R                          |
|                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing             |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : G = genericMatrix(R,3,3)   |
|                                |
|o2 = | x_(1,1) x_(2,1) x_(3,1) ||
|     | x_(1,2) x_(2,2) x_(3,2) ||
|     | x_(1,3) x_(2,3) x_(3,3) ||
|                                |
|             3      3           |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+

Since $X_0$ is a single point, its first jet scheme consists of a single
(smooth) point.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I1 = minors(1,G)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = ideal (x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   )            |
|             1,1   1,2   1,3   2,1   2,2   2,3   3,1   3,2   3,3             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : JI1 = jets(1,I1)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = ideal (x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   ,   |
|              1,1    1,1    1,2    1,2    1,3    1,3    2,1    2,1    2,2    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   , x1   , x0   )          |
|       2,2    2,3    2,3    3,1    3,1    3,2    3,2    3,3    3,3           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[x0   ..x0   ][x1   ..x1   ]                                 |
|                   1,1    3,3    1,1    3,3                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : dim JI1, isPrime JI1                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = (0, true)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
